{{Term/Store|Stalmoblin|Stalmoblins|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC|plural}} are recurring [[Boss]]es and [[Enemy|Enemies]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Stalmoblin'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Stalmoblin'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|'''Stalmoblin'''}}|Game Screen|AoC}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Stalmoblin}}
Stalmoblins are the skeletal remains of [[Moblin]]s that emerge from the ground at night.<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|The remains of Moblins appear in the dark of the night. Even the toughest Moblins become fragile when they're little more than a pile of bones, so they'll crumble after just a few attacks. However, as long as a skull remains intact, they'll continue to pull themselves back together and go on fighting.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> They may have various [[Weapon]]s equipped, but if they do not, they will attempt to strike [[Link]] with his fists. Like other [[Stal]] [[Enemy|Enemies]], their bones are very fragile and any attack from Link will cause them to fall apart.<ref name="Compendium"/> The bones rebuild themselves without the head after a short period of time and walk toward any disembodied head, and at the same time, the head will attempt to hop towards the body.<ref name="Compendium"/> After being broken apart, Link can pick up a Stalmoblin's [[Moblin Arm]] and use it as a Weapon.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Moblin Arm}}<br/>A Moblin bone that continues to move even after being detached from its body. The bone is thick enough to be used as a weapon but is extremely brittle and easily broken.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref> If Link destroys the head before the [[Monster]] rebuilds itself, it will be permanently defeated and both the body and head will vanish. When defeated, they drop [[Moblin Fang]]s and [[Moblin Horn]]s.

If Link wears the [[Moblin Mask]], [[Majora's Mask (Item)|Majora's Mask]], or possesses the [[Disguise; Bone Atk. Up]] [[Set Bonus]] by wearing the full [[Radiant Set]] or [[Phantom Ganon Set]], Stalmoblins will not attack him unless he attacks first.

